        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="swimlane;html=1;startSize=32;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;swimlaneFillColor=#ffffff;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;arcSize=3;strokeWidth=2;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;" value="Changes vs Microsoft&#39;s graphic" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="970" x="580" y="1010" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notesT" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;" value="&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt; Every item sits on a labelled path — nothing floats. Real-Time Hub redrawn as a catalog plane (it stores no data), not a flow node.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt; Activator&#39;s real inputs made explicit: Eventstream destination, direct Fabric/Azure events, and alert rules from KQL Queryset, Real-Time Dashboard and Power BI.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt; Lakehouse added as an Eventstream destination; Eventhouse ↔ OneLake shown both ways (OneLake availability out, accelerated shortcuts in).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt; Generic source icons replaced by named source classes, incl. 2026 additions: Oracle CDC, Mirrored DB change feed, business events, DeltaFlow, Spark Structured Streaming.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt; Digital twin builder kept in RTI (still preview) and wired to its lake input; Fabric IQ (Ontology, Data agent, Operations agent) and Fabric Maps added as RTI consumers." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="945" x="595" y="1047" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
